.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt TPROMPT 1
.Os tprompt 0.2.0
.Sh NAME
.Nm tprompt
.Nd prompt for named inputs, print name=value lines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | Fl V
.Op Fl -in-shell | Fl -new-shell | Fl -popup
.Op Fl -interactive | Fl -scripted
.Op Fl -picker Ar fzf Ns | Ns Ar numbered Ns | Ns Ar cmd
.Op Fl -no-tmux
.Op Fl -no-fzf
.Op Fl -color Op Li = Ns Ar always Ns | Ns Ar auto Ns | Ns Ar never
.Op Fl -multi
.Op Fl -sep Ar char
.Op Fl -trim | Fl -no-trim
.Op Fl -validate Ar regex
.Op Fl -retry Ar n
.Op Fl -header Ar text
.Op Fl -width Ar n
.Op Fl -height Ar n
.Op Fl -auto-size
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -json-array
.Op Fl -label-color Ar spec
.Op Fl -default-color Ar spec
.Op Fl -theme Ar name
.Op Fl -save Ar file
.Op Fl -load Ar file
.Op Fl -multiline
.Op Fl -sentinel Ar s
.Op Fl -timeout Ar n
.Op Fl -history Ar file
.Op Fl -print-spec
.Op Fl -specs-from Ar file
.Op Ar spec ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
collects one or more named inputs from the user and prints one
.Sq Li name=value
line per input, in order, to stdout.
It is standalone (no
.Xr tum 1
dependency), tmux-optional, and fzf-optional.
.Pp
Inputs are described in one of two forms:
.Bl -tag -width "B (positional)"
.It B (positional)
Each argument is
.Ql name|prompt|default[|values] .
Repeatable for multiple inputs.
A leading
.Ql *
on the name marks a secret (hidden entry); a leading
.Ql !
marks a required field (an empty answer is an error).
The prefixes combine
.Pq Ql *! Ns or Ql !*
and are stripped from the output key.
A
.Ql qr:
prefixed field at any position is a validation regex (see
.Sx VALIDATION );
a
.Ql pv:
prefixed field at any position is a preview command (see
.Sx PREVIEW );
a
.Ql file:
prefixed default opens an editor.
.It C (stdin)
When no B positionals are given and stdin is not a tty, a spec is read from
stdin as
.Ql key=value
lines, with a blank line separating inputs.
Recognized keys:
.Li name ,
.Li prompt ,
.Li default ,
.Li values ,
.Li default-env ,
.Li values-env ,
.Li secret ,
.Li multi ,
.Li trim ,
.Li required ,
.Li validate ,
.Li validate-error ,
.Li label-color ,
.Li default-color ,
.Li preview .
.El
.Pp
In
.Ar values ,
a comma-separated list turns the input into a pick (fzf or numbered).
With
.Fl -multi
(or C
.Li multi=1 )
the user may select several; selected values are joined with
.Fl -sep
(default
.Ql , ) .
.Sq Ev $VAR
and
.Sq Ev ${VAR}
are expanded in
.Li default ,
.Li values ,
and
.Li prompt
from the environment.
.Sh SECRET INPUT
A leading
.Ql *
on the name marks the input as secret.
Entry is hidden
.Pq Ic stty -echo ,
the default is not shown in the prompt (it would leak it), and the
.Ql *
is stripped so the output key is the bare name.
If the user enters an empty line, the default is used silently.
The output is still cleartext
.Pq Li pw=s3cr3t :
.Nm
hides
.Em entry ,
not the captured value.
In C, use
.Li name=*pw
or the
.Li secret=1
key.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-picker fzf|numbered|cmd"
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show usage and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print version and exit.
.It Fl -in-shell
Prompt in the current shell (default without tmux).
.It Fl -new-shell
Prompt in a fresh shell; uses a tmux popup if available, else in-shell.
.It Fl -popup
Prompt in a tmux
.Ic display-popup .
Requires being inside tmux; otherwise degrades to
.Fl -in-shell
with a stderr notice.
.It Fl -no-tmux
Never use tmux (popup/new-shell degrade to in-shell silently).
.It Fl -interactive
Force prompting (default when stdin is a tty).
.It Fl -scripted
Force non-interactive (default when stdin is a pipe).
.It Fl -picker Ar fzf | numbered | Ar cmd
Picker for values-list inputs.
.Li fzf
(the default when installed),
.Li numbered ,
or an external command that reads a newline-list on stdin and prints the
choice on stdout.
.It Fl -no-fzf
Never use fzf; force numbered.
.It Fl -multi
Allow multiple values per values-list input.
Interactive fzf uses
.Ic --multi ;
the numbered picker reads a comma-separated line of indices or literal values.
Selected values are joined with
.Fl -sep .
Free-text inputs (no values list) are unaffected.
.It Fl -sep Ar char
Separator for joined multi-values (default
.Ql , ) .
Multi-character separators are accepted.
.Fl -separator
is a long alias.
.It Fl -color Op Li = Ns Ar always | auto | never
Colorize the prompt label (bold cyan) and the default hint (dim yellow) on
stderr.
Bare
.Fl -color
means
.Ar always ;
the default is
.Ar auto
(on when stderr is a tty and
.Ev NO_COLOR
is unset).
ANSI codes in a
.Li values
list are rendered in the picker and stripped from the output, so
.Li name=value
is always plain text.
.It Fl -label-color Ar spec
Set the prompt-label color.
.It Fl -default-color Ar spec
Set the default-hint color.
A spec is a named color
.Po Li black , Li red , Li green , Li yellow , Li blue , Li magenta , Li cyan , Li white Pc
with optional styles
.Po Li bold , Li dim , Li underline Pc ,
combinable as
.Ql bold red ,
or a raw SGR string like
.Ql 1;31 .
.It Fl -theme Ar name
Bundle label and default colors:
.Li default ,
.Li dark ,
.Li light ,
.Li high-contrast .
C
.Li label-color= Ns / Ns Li default-color=
keys override per spec.
The on/off
.Fl -color
switch gates all of this.
.It Fl -trim
Trim leading and trailing whitespace from answers.
Default is on for non-secrets and off for secrets
(a secret with trailing spaces is a real case).
.Fl -no-trim
preserves whitespace.
A C
.Li trim=0 Ns / Ns Li trim=1
key overrides per spec.
Trimming runs after the read and before validation.
.It Fl -validate Ar regex
A POSIX ERE every free-text answer must match.
A mismatch is an error in scripted mode and a cancel in interactive mode.
A per-spec regex
.Po B
.Ql qr:
field at any position, or C
.Li validate=
.Pc
overrides this for one input and also applies to values-list picks;
picks are otherwise exempt
.Pq valid by construction .
.Fl -validate-error Ar msg
overrides the default
.Ql invalid: does not match <pattern>
message.
Checked after
.Fl -required .
.It Fl -retry Ar n
Re-prompt up to
.Ar n
times on a
.Fl -required
or
.Fl -validate
failure before canceling
.Pq default 0 , fail fast .
A C
.Li retry= Ns Ar n
key overrides per spec.
The counter is per-input.
Scripted mode ignores
.Fl -retry
.Pq no re-prompt loop over a pipe
with a stderr notice.
Each retry prints
.Ql invalid: <reason>; try again (n left)
on stderr.
.It Fl -header Ar text
A banner printed to stderr once before the first prompt
.Pq colored with the label color when Fl -color is on ;
for fzf it is also passed as fzf
.Ql Fl -header .
.Fl -header-file Ar path
reads the banner from a file; the two are mutually exclusive and a missing file
is a hard error.
Multi-line banners are supported.
.It Fl -width Ar n
Tmux popup width in characters
.Pq default 80 .
.It Fl -height Ar n
Tmux popup height in lines
.Pq default 20 .
.It Fl -auto-size
Compute the popup width and height from the specs
.Po max prompt+default+value width, number of inputs plus padding Pc ,
capped at the terminal size.
In-shell mode ignores these
.Pq there is no popup .
.It Fl -json
Emit JSON Lines: one
.Ql {"name":"...","value":"..."}
object per input, on its own line, instead of
.Ql name=value .
.It Fl -json-array
Emit a single JSON array on one line
.Pq implies Fl -json .
Values are JSON-escaped; secrets are cleartext.
Multi-values stay a single joined string.
.It Fl -save Ar file
Write this run's
.Li name=value
answers to
.Ar file
on success
.Pq atomic: temp plus rename .
Secrets are skipped
.Pq with a stderr warning
unless
.Fl -save-secrets
is given.
.It Fl -load Ar file
Pre-fill defaults from a prior answers file
.Po Li # comments and blank lines ignored Pc ;
a missing file is a silent no-op.
Precedence: typed answer \*[Gt] loaded value \*[Gt] spec default.
.Fl -json
and
.Fl -save
are mutually exclusive.
A missing parent directory or non-writable
.Fl -save
target is a hard error.
.It Fl -multiline
Read a multi-line block until a sentinel line
.Po default Ql . ; Fl -sentinel Ar s sets it, Ql Fl -sentinel= means EOF-terminated Pc .
Blank lines are part of the block; the sentinel is excluded.
C
.Li multiline=1 Ns / Ns Li sentinel=
per spec.
Values-list inputs ignore it.
.It Fl -timeout Ar n
Cancel the run after
.Ar n
seconds
.Po a background alarm + SIGALRM trap Pc .
A timeout is a cancel
.Pq exit non-zero, no stdout .
Does not fire if input arrives in time.
.It Fl -history Ar file
Pre-fill each input's default with the last prior value for its name from
.Ar file ,
and append this run's
.Li name=value
answers on success
.Po secrets skipped unless Fl -save-secrets Pc .
A missing file is created on append.
.It Fl -print-spec
Normalize specs only, print sixteen tab-separated columns
.Pq Li name , Li prompt , Li default , Li values , Li secret , Li multi , Li trim , Li required , Li validate , Li validate-error , Li retry , Li label-color , Li default-color , Li preview , Li multiline , Li sentinel ,
and exit. Debug.
.It Fl -specs-from Ar file
Read B specs from
.Ar file
(one per line;
.Ql #
comments and blank lines are ignored) instead of positional args.
Mutually exclusive with B positionals; combines with C (stdin is then the
answer pipe for scripted B, or a tty for interactive B).
A missing, unreadable, or spec-free file is a hard error (exit 1), unlike
.Fl -load
which is optional pre-fill.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT
One
.Ql name=value
line per input, in order, on stdout.
Prompts and the numbered list go to stderr.
On cancel (Esc in fzf, EOF/Ctrl-D on a prompt, or a malformed spec),
.Nm
exits non-zero and prints nothing on stdout.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "1-2"
.It 0
All inputs collected; results on stdout.
.It 1
Cancel, or an error (e.g. an input with no resolvable default in scripted mode).
.It 2
Usage error.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "TPROMPT_BIN"
.It Ev TMUX
If set (inside tmux) and
.Xr tmux 1
is available, the default render mode is
.Fl -popup .
.It Ev NO_COLOR
If set, disables color in
.Ar auto
mode.
.It Ev TPROMPT_BIN
Used by the test suite to locate the binary.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width "tprompt --multi --sep , 'tags|t||a,b,c,d'"
.It Nm Ql host|host to probe|localhost
Prompt for one input with a default.
.It Nm Ql port|port|22|22,80,443
Prompt for an input chosen from a values list.
.It Nm Ql *pw|Password:
Prompt for a secret (hidden entry); the
.Ql *
is stripped.
.It Nm Fl -multi Fl -sep Ql , Ql tags|t||a,b,c,d
Allow several values from the list, joined with
.Ql , .
.It Nm Fl -color=always Ql host|h|localhost
Colorize the prompt label and default hint.
.It Nm Fl -print-spec Ql k|k|$USER
Show the normalized record (default column expands
.Ev $USER ) .
.It Nm Fl -specs-from Ar deploy.txt
Read B specs (one per line) from a file instead of argv.
.El
